<!--
  EXTRACTION.md — the manifest of what got mined from THIS pack into the brain.
  Every pack under packs/ needs one (verified by scripts/verify-packs.sh).
  The purpose: retrieval attribution. When brain.sh recall surfaces a lesson,
  we know which pack it came from and can measure that pack's contribution.

  Copy this file to packs/<your-pack>/EXTRACTION.md and fill it in.
  If a section has nothing to extract, keep the heading and write "None."
  Do NOT delete unused sections — an explicit "None" is a claim, an absent
  section reads as "not yet examined".
-->

# EXTRACTION — `<pack-name>`

- **Upstream:** `<url>` @ `<pinned-sha>`
- **First mined:** `<YYYY-MM-DD>`
- **Last re-mined:** `<YYYY-MM-DD>` (against upstream SHA `<sha>`)
- **Extractor:** `<who / which pass>`

## Rationale — why this pack is in the harness

One paragraph. What unique contribution does this pack make that other
packs don't? If you can't answer this in a paragraph, the pack should be
`.deprecated`.

## Extracted lessons

Each row: one atomic, retrievable lesson. Attribution goes on the brain
line itself so `brain.sh recall <target>` surfaces the source.

| Brain record | Class | Title (≤80 chars) | Source file |
|---|---|---|---|
| `brain/lessons.md:L<line>` | `<class>` | `<title>` | `packs/<pack>/<file>:<line>` |

*If none: write `None.` — the pack had no novel lessons worth folding.*

## Extracted payloads

Each row: a payload set folded into `brain/payloads/<class>.txt`, with the
line range so re-mining can dedupe.

| Brain file | Line range | Count | Source file |
|---|---|---|---|
| `brain/payloads/<class>.txt` | `L<start>-L<end>` | `<N>` | `packs/<pack>/<file>` |

*If none: write `None.`*

## Extracted tools

Each row: a tool registered in `brain/tools.md`.

| Brain record | Tool name | Purpose (≤60 chars) | Source file |
|---|---|---|---|
| `brain/tools.md:L<line>` | `<name>` | `<purpose>` | `packs/<pack>/<file>:<line>` |

*If none: write `None.`*

## Extracted patterns (conditional triggers)

Patterns fire on `brain.sh recall-class <class>` — they say "if you see X,
try Y". Not narrative lessons — atomic {precondition, action} pairs.

| ID | Class | Precondition | Action | Source |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `PAT-<pack>-<n>` | `<class>` | `<what triggers this>` | `<what to try>` | `packs/<pack>/<file>` |

*If none: write `None.`*

## Router integration

- `references/router.md:L<line>` — how this pack is routed

If the pack has no router entry (marked `.internal`), explain here why —
e.g. "runtime-only, dispatched by scripts/foo.sh, not by /mad-hunt".

## Verification (last run)

- Last `scripts/verify-packs.sh` result: `<PASS|FAIL>` at `<date>`
- Last drift check vs upstream: `<pinned SHA>` == `<remote HEAD>`? `<yes|no>`
- If drift: `<what changed, whether re-mining pending>`

## Notes / next re-mining

Anything a future re-mining pass should know — filters that missed content,
categories to look at more carefully, upstream branches to watch.
